verbs answer on the gdi lane for the first time.

ROUND 1 -- one HIGH, real, mine.
  H1  s_flips is not a frame counter. I handed the family the flip
      count and their `% 5` throttles were written against the ~60/s
      present rate; the shell flips ~12,000 times a second (measured on
      MAINMENU). A ~100x rate increase on five file-writing observers.
      The evidence was in CENSUS_MS's own comment, twenty lines above
      where I inserted the call -- I read past it.
      FIXED (45b3a5e): a TRIG_MS 16 QPC gate with its own counter.

ROUND 2 -- no HIGH. Two MEDIUMs, both documentation, both applied (ae88b17).
  It verified rather than assumed, and that is what it is for:
    - the gate's arithmetic and lifecycle: 16 ms -> 62.5/s; the epoch is
      not advanced past the deadline, so no drift accumulates; the
      commit's claimed 1.27 file stats per flip is exact
      (1/15 + 1/5 + 1/5 + 2/5 + 2/5 = 1.267).
    - the counter is equivalent: no modulo can be skipped, a freeze is
      not a hazard, and tacli never reads the "frame" field.
    - THE HAZARD CLOSURE IS TRUE -- by independent sweep, not by reading
      my row. Every file naming main+0x1439B / OFF_UNITDEFS, every deref
      of unit+0x92, and an objdump of 0x491b60..0x491c60 showing none of
      the teardown cascade's 22 calls reaches the flip at 0x4C63A0.
  M1  cross-thread-engine-reads.md -- the 2026-09-11 audit, and the note
      of record the closed row CITES -- still said in three places that
      these six read engine memory on the render thread. Five of the six
      no longer do.
  M2  tagpu_reclaim.c's reader list was missing tagpu_packet_pub, and
      the paragraph claimed every reader was on the game thread while
      three were not. It is now true AND complete, with the sweep named.
  LOW/NIT applied: the gate fails CLOSED where the census gate beside it
